**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Author:** Codex with gniadzikm

## Context

The rendered views of #4471 contradict its single-cause summary. Subject equality concealed
different parser and form-hint defects. Different subjects also described the same defect.

## Decision

This record supersedes [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) for new triage.
Read the report body and establish tenant locale, form version and channel.
Merge only when evidence supports the same cause. Use `causeOf` and `sameCause` as the current
routing model, not as proof that every narrative is explained. Do not use intake tags or browser
locale as substitutes for the tenant directory. Unknown or contradictory evidence needs review.

## Consequences

Triage requires reading rather than subject-only matching. Engineering receives separate
parser and hint work, with unique report counts. The one-day narratives remain visible for
investigation rather than being silently declared explained or labeled a proven timezone bug.
This is the proposed desk rule in this submitted kb; no live support policy was changed here.

See the [signed review](/kb/incidents/4471-review/) for rendered evidence.

